<title>Australia: Australian stocks seen continuing firmer run.</title>
<headline>Australian stocks seen continuing firmer run.</headline>
<text>
<p>-----------------(Snapshot 8.50 a.m./2250 GMT)-----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	   2488.00   +8.90   DJIA  cl	7008.99  +49.46</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl	 2500	+4   US 30yr cl	 6.96   -0.02</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    92.160  +0.025   Gold NY 339.55 Lon fix 340.15</p>
<p>AUD	   0.7812 (Wed 0.7813)   CRB Index cl   248.29   +1.61</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	19151.12 +480.75   FTSE cl	 4436.00   +2.80</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   802.70   -0.10   NZSE40	  2255.53   -6.41</p>
<p>--------------------------(May 1)------------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks seen adding to recent gains as Dow firms again.</p>
<p>&quot;There is some more in it for us. We keep creeping ahead without</p>
<p>too much drama,&quot; said a dealer at a Sydney brokerage.</p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$18.15 (+.07), A$17.50 (-.05), A$5.90 (-.01), A$7.59 (-.01)</p>
<p>*U.S. stocks steamrolled higher, staging a broad advance that took the Dow back above the 7,000 level.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 18-1/2 (-1/4), BHP 28-3/8 (+1/4), WMC 24 (-1/8), National Australia Bank 68-7/8 (+1/2)</p>
<p>*Gold price was firmer. On LME copper charged higher with the rest of the complex riding its coat tails although only aluminium saw much activity.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
